  "body": "Stacked on #4139 (merge #4139 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- The Sodick LN2W post (`assets/posts/sodick-ln2w.cps`) now posts a constant taper. It uses the 4-axis form that the owner of an AQ600L uses (his input on #4075, 2026-11-25).\n- The start order of #4065 does not change: `G54`, `G00 X Y U0. V0.`, `Z0.`, `T91`, `T84`, `T94`, the `C` word.\n- After the `C` word, the post writes `TP`, `TN` and `G74`. Then each cut is `G01 X Y U V`. `G75` comes after the last cut, before `T90`.\n- `X Y` is the wire's point on the part's bottom. `U V` is the part's top minus its bottom.\n- `TP` is the cut's bottom above the worktable. `TN` is `TP` plus the cut's height.\n- `TP` follows the section's own `WireBottom` (review round 1). The option is the `TP` of the first tapered cut of the program. A later tapered cut gets `TP` = the option + (its `WireBottom` - the first `WireBottom`). The post refuses by name a `TP` below the worktable.\n- Each section note names the work Z of its `TP` and the work Z that the option states. Example: `TP 13. IS WORK Z8. ABOVE THE WORKTABLE - THE POST OPTION STATES WORK Z0. AT 5.`\n- CamCraft does not know the fixture height. The user sets it in a new declared post option, `partBottomAboveTable` (\"Part bottom above the worktable (mm)\"). The default is -1 (not stated). When it is not stated, the post refuses each taper by name. The existing undoable command `SetPostScriptOptions` and its MCP tool set the option. No new command is necessary.\n- The app (`crates/app/src/posting_wire.rs`) sends four new PARAMs before a guide-offset leaning section: `WireGuideLower`, `WireGuideUpper`, `WireBottom`, `WireTop` (work Z, mm). The post uses them to move U V from the guide planes to the part's planes along the same straight wire. `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` has the new row. The other wire posts ignore these PARAMs.\n- The post refuses by name:\n  - the angle form (`G51` / `G52` `A`, `G50`): the corner motion is not confirmed, and the owner does not use it;\n  - a taper from a second setup (the option holds one height for the program);\n  - an arc in a tapered cut;\n  - the control's wire offset (G41 / G42) in a tapered cut;\n  - a tapered cut that ends with the wire leaning (G75 needs the wire upright);\n  - a stream that does not state the four planes.\n- A 4-axis cut with two profiles (`WireFourAxis`) stays refused.\n- Documentation: the machine file description, `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`, the user guide (`machines.md`), and `docs/decisions/4075-ln2w-4axis-taper.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nBefore this change, the post refused each taper (#4065). The open items were the table height (item 1), the corner motion under G51 / G52 (item 2), the lean side (item 3) and the angle precision (item 4). In the 4-axis form CamCraft decides each corner, so item 2 does not apply. The lean side is the sign of U V, from the geometry. No angle word is written, so item 4 does not apply.\n\n## Smallest change for the table height\n\nThe issue asks for a per-setup value with a command and an MCP tool (item 1). The brief asked for the smallest change when the machine file does not state the heights (#2130). I used a declared post option. It is safe for a one-setup program, and the post refuses tapers from two setups by name. A per-setup value can replace it later. The decision file records this.\n\n## Tests (pins, mutation results)\n\nNew pins, `crates/post/tests/sodick_ln2w/taper.rs` (binary `script_sodick_ln2w`):\n- `a_taper_posts_as_a_four_axis_program_with_tp_tn_and_uv_on_every_move`\n- `the_lean_side_is_the_sign_of_u_and_v`\n- `a_taper_without_the_table_height_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_taper_stream_without_its_planes_is_refused_by_name`\n- `tapers_from_two_setups_are_refused_by_name`\n- `an_arc_or_a_wire_offset_in_a_taper_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_taper_that_ends_leaning_is_refused_by_name`\n- `tp_follows_each_tapered_sections_own_bottom` (review round 1: two tapered sections in one setup, `WireBottom` 0 and 8; the second gets `TP13.` `TN25.`; also the reverse order)\n- `a_tapered_section_below_the_worktable_is_refused_by_name` (review round 1)\n\nApp pins, `crates/app/tests/wire_post/sodick_aq600l.rs` (binary `wire_post`):\n- `the_ln2w_taper_part_posts_as_a_four_axis_program_with_the_table_height` (new golden `edm_test_taper.nc`)\n- `the_ln2w_taper_part_is_refused_by_name_without_the_table_height` (replaces the old refusal test)\n\nMutation checks:\n- The unchanged post with the new pins: all 7 post pins fail (red).\n- The unchanged `posting_wire.rs` with the new post: the two app pins fail (red): \"the stream states no PARAM WireGuideLower\".\n- Review round 1, `tpOf()` returns only the option (the old `TP`): the two new pins fail (red).\n- Review round 1, no refusal of a `TP` below the worktable: `a_tapered_section_below_the_worktable_is_refused_by_name` fails (red).\n- Restored: all pins pass (green).\n\nThe golden was checked by hand. The bottom of the punch is 50 x 30 mm, and the top is 44 x 24 mm over 20 mm. The kerf is 0.165 mm, or 0.165 / cos(8.53 deg) = 0.167 mm on the floor. So the bottom wire is at X +-25.167, and the U V lean is 3 mm inward on each wall: U3 on the -X wall, U-3 on the +X wall. Each corner is a mitre that CamCraft states.\n\nResults on the final head (`768fb3231`, against `upstream/main` `e6849c5ae`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 853 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (51.3 min). This includes `script_sodick_ln2w`, `wire_post` and the catalog suites `example_catalog` (43 passed), `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed (6.9 min, on the final head).\n- Heavy: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reaches 72 release steps. This is a P6 PR, so by AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" it gets no full heavy lane. I ran the one targeted step of the changed binary: `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: wire_post\"`: 1 step, 0 failed (on the final head).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- New: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-ln2w/edm_test_taper.nc`. Review round 1 changed its taper note line only (the note now names the work Z). I made it again with `WRITE_GOLDEN`. No executable word changed.\n- No other golden changed. The non-taper output is byte-identical: `edm_test_square.nc` and `edm_test_2axis.nc` pass with no change, and the other wire posts' suites pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The output was not run on a Sodick control. The owner must check `TP` / `TN` / `G74` / `G75` on the machine graphics before a cut.\n- The order of `TP` / `TN` / `G74` after the `C` word is my choice. The owner gave the words, not their exact position. It keeps the start order of #4065.\n- A per-setup table height (item 1 as written) is not done. See above.\n- `crates/app/src/posting_wire.rs` was 417 lines before this PR and is 425 now. I did not split it here, to keep the diff small.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #4139 (`issue/4076-ln2w-wire-offset`). It changes the same post (`offsetStep`, `onLinear`). Merge #4139 first.\n- #3617 touches other wire files, not this post.\n\nChangelog: The Sodick LN2W post writes a constant taper as a 4-axis program (TP / TN, G74, U V on every move, G75); set the post option \"Part bottom above the worktable\" first.\n\nFixes #4075\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
